          deckDescription: "One standard 52-card deck consisting of four suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs), each with thirteen ranks from ace down to two. No jokers; used for Boerenbridge (farmer's bridge) where all ranks are active and the game is a simplified contract bridge for four players.",
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). Trump is determined by the contract or bid; follow suit when able. Standard trick order applies; the declarer and dummy work as in bridge with a reduced rule set.',
          rankDescription: 'Thirteen ranks per suit: ace high, then king, queen, jack, ten, nine, eight, seven, six, five, four, three, two low. Standard trick-taking order; no card is stripped. Contract and declarer play follow Boerenbridge rules.',
          dealPattern: 'Individually clockwise until hand is full.',
          bettingLimits: 'None',
          actions: {},
